Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================================
;  REVERT: restore TDR to the disabled state this machine had before
; ============================================================================
;  Only use this if re-enabling TDR caused a problem — for example if long
;  generations are being killed mid-run by the 10 second timeout.
;
;  Better first step than reverting: raise TdrDelay (e.g. 30 or 60) while
;  KEEPING TdrLevel = 3, so hang detection stays on but tolerates longer
;  kernels. Reverting to TdrLevel = 0 restores the condition where any GPU
;  hang takes down the whole machine.
;
;  REQUIRES A REBOOT to take effect.
; ============================================================================

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers]
"TdrLevel"=dword:00000000
"TdrDelay"=dword:00000078
